PARITY NOTES (web Tabs.tsx → native; every branch reproduced)
  • web controlled `activeTab` + `onChange`     → SwiftUI `Binding<String>` (value+setter
    IS the controlled contract; arrow/Home/End auto-activate by writing the binding —
    web "automatic activation").
  • web roving `tabIndex` + `handleKeyDown`      → @FocusState roving focus + .onKeyPress
    (.leftArrow/.rightArrow/.home/.end) → pure TabsKeyboardNavigation. Disabled tabs are
    `.disabled` so focus skips them (web enabledKeys). The "single tab stop" roving-
    tabindex nuance maps imperfectly to SwiftUI focus; it is approximated via the tested
    `initialFocusKey` (documented, not silent drift).
  • web `useId()` ids                            → TabsIdentity.tabID/panelID, surfaced as
    accessibility identifiers; a per-instance base (web useId) via @State, overridable.
  • web container `border-b` / selected `border-b-2` → 1pt bottom rule (Color.TS.border) +
    a 2pt accent underline on the selected tab.
  • web blue (`text/border-blue-600`)            → Color.TS.accent token (theme-correct in
    light/dark/high-contrast); idle/hover → textMuted/textSecondary (web hover:text-gray).
  • web empty `tabs.map([])`                     → TabsEmptyState (never a blank box).
  • web has NO loading/error/stale/offline       → native widenings the Apple surface
    contract requires, rendered as real chrome (documented), per the AnomalyInlineRow
    precedent. No Tailwind class ported — platform tokens only (P1/S9).
  • Charts/maps: NONE in the web source — nothing to port to Swift Charts / MapKit.

